Module500124Name = Advanced TakePOS
Module500124Desc = TakePOS customizations via hooks (stock, public price + %, price level, font)
AdvancedTakeposSetup = Advanced TakePOS setup
AdvancedTakeposSetupPage = Each option below turns on a customization carried by hooks, without modifying the core.
#
# Options
#
AdvTakeposShowStock = Show stock of products
AdvTakeposShowStockHelp = Shows the stock held by the warehouse of the terminal, and the stock of all warehouses when the two differ, on a dedicated badge.
AdvTakeposShowPublicPrice = Show public price of products
AdvTakeposShowPublicPriceHelp = When the customer is on a price level other than the public one, shows the public price next to the price charged.
AdvTakeposShowPriceDiff = Show sale/public price difference %
AdvTakeposShowPriceDiffHelp = Appends the percentage difference between the price charged and the public price.
AdvTakeposPublicPriceLevel = Price level used as reference
AdvTakeposPublicPriceLevelHelp = The level whose price is shown as the "public price" next to the price charged, and used as the base for the difference percentage. Defaults to level 1. Change it when level 1 holds the current tariff and the recommended public price lives on another level.
AdvTakeposLevelN = Level %s
AdvTakeposPublicPriceShort = RRP
AdvTakeposLinePublicPriceCol = Reference price column on receipt lines
AdvTakeposLinePublicPriceColHelp = Adds a receipt column with the reference level price, **tax included** (the core unit price column is tax excluded). Its title uses the reference level name when one is set. A dash means the product has no price on that level.
AdvTakeposUnitPriceTtc = Receipt unit price including tax
AdvTakeposUnitPriceTtcHelp = The native unit price column, which TakePOS shows excluding tax, shows each line's unit price including tax. Inert while that column is hidden (TakePOS option "TAKEPOS_SHOW_SUBPRICE").
AdvTakeposLineAtPublicPrice = Charge the line at the reference price, gap as a discount
AdvTakeposLineAtPublicPriceHelp = When a line is added, the unit price becomes the reference level price and the gap with the customer tariff is carried as a discount percentage. The net amount is unchanged; the receipt reads "reference price - discount = net" and discount statistics become usable. Inert while the reference level is the customer level, or when the line already carries a discount.
AdvTakeposPromoLevel = Promo level, gap as a discount
AdvTakeposPromoLevelHelp = When a line is added, the unit price stays at the customer tariff (the shop price) and the gap down to this level price is carried as a discount percentage, when this level has a lower price. The receipt reads "shop price - discount = promo price". A discount already set is never overwritten. Inert when the product has no price on this level. When a promo price applies, it takes precedence over "Charge the line at the reference price".
AdvTakeposShowLevelInTitle = Show price level in the title bar
AdvTakeposShowLevelInTitleHelp = Shows the terminal price level and its label in the top bar.
AdvTakeposFullwidthNoCat = Full-width products when categories are hidden
AdvTakeposFullwidthNoCatHelp = Fixes the v24 display: when categories are hidden, products take the whole width.
AdvTakeposSmallerFont = Reduce product font size
AdvTakeposSmallerFontHelp = Reduces the character size on product tiles to fit everything.
AdvTakeposHideTerminalDate = Hide terminal date
AdvTakeposHideTerminalDateHelp = Hides the date shown after the terminal name in the title bar.
AdvTakeposHideCurrency = Hide currency selector
AdvTakeposHideCurrencyHelp = Hides the "Currency" button in the title bar (without disabling the multicurrency module).
AdvTakeposCartCustomer = Customer name in cart tooltips
AdvTakeposCartCustomerHelp = Adds the customer name to the tooltip (hover) of each open cart in the title bar.
AdvTakeposDeleteSale = Delete sale
AdvTakeposDeleteSaleOpt = "Delete sale" button
AdvTakeposDeleteSaleOptHelp = Adds a button to the action bar to delete (with confirmation) the current cart.
AdvTakeposCompactActions = Compact action buttons
AdvTakeposCompactActionsHelp = Reduces the action buttons width to the numpad keys width (4 per row).
AdvTakeposLightHeader = Light title bar
AdvTakeposLightHeaderHelp = Hides the warehouse and stretches the search bar to the maximum (icons pushed to the right).
AdvTakeposEditPopup = Qty / Price / Discount input popup
AdvTakeposEditPopupHelp = Replaces the native input (written under the selected line) with a numeric-pad popup, modeled on the vendor popup.
AdvTakeposPager = Products pager
AdvTakeposPagerHelp = Floating buttons to turn product pages (categories and search results). Page size follows TAKEPOS_NB_MAXPRODUCT (N-2 products).
#
# Misc (rendering)
#
AdvTakeposStockHelp = Stock held by the warehouse of the terminal, and total stock across all warehouses when the two differ.
AdvTakeposLevel = Level
AdvTakeposParams = Parameters
AdvTakeposInputMode = Qty / Price / Discount input mode
AdvTakeposInputModeHelp = Native: raw text under the line. Native + focus: on-screen keypad kept, the value shows in a clean badge anchored on the line. Popup: modal with its own pad. Popup only: the modal handles everything, the on-screen keypad shrinks to Qty / Price / Line discount / C / trash.
AdvTakeposIMNative = Native
AdvTakeposIMInline = Native keypad + focus badge
AdvTakeposIMPopup = Popup + full keypad
AdvTakeposIMPopupOnly = Popup only (reduced keypad)
AdvTakeposPriceDiscountMode = Entering a price: what about the discount?
AdvTakeposPriceDiscountModeHelp = What to do with the existing discount when a new price is entered in the popup: keep it (applied on top, native), reset it to zero (entered price = paid price), or convert the entered price into a discount percent (catalog price kept, discount statistics preserved).
AdvTakeposPDModeNative = Keep discount (native)
AdvTakeposPDModeReset = Reset discount (entered price = paid price)
AdvTakeposPDModeConvert = Convert to discount (catalog price kept)
AdvTakeposDesktopPreset = Desktop grid (preset)
AdvTakeposDesktopPresetHelp = A: 24 products in 3×8, native arrows replaced by the pager. B: 30 products in 3×10 (narrower tiles). C: pure native, 22 products + 2 arrows. Manual: use the fields below.
AdvTakeposPresetManual = Manual
AdvTakeposPresetA = A — 24 products (3×8 + pager)
AdvTakeposPresetB = B — 30 products (3×10 + pager)
AdvTakeposPresetC = C — 22 products (native)
AdvTakeposPagerPos = Pager position
AdvTakeposPagerPosHelp = Floating: round buttons at the bottom-right of the products area. Under action buttons: embedded in the actions column (visible on all screens).
AdvTakeposPagerFloat = Floating on products
AdvTakeposPagerUnderActions = Under the action buttons
AdvTakeposGridMobile = Product grid slots — mobile
AdvTakeposGridTablet = Product grid slots — tablet (768-1024)
AdvTakeposGridDesktop = Product grid slots — desktop/tablet
AdvTakeposGridHelp = Number of grid slots (N-2 products + 2 arrows), specific to each device: the value is stored in the browser and applied to its TakePOS pages without changing TAKEPOS_NB_MAXPRODUCT, so a phone and a large screen each keep their own grid. 0 = not managed (TakePOS value).
AdvTakeposProductCardPopup = Product card popup (tile, line, F2)
AdvTakeposProductCardPopupHelp = Info icon on each product tile; on ticket lines, click the reference or the native info picto (its hover tooltip is kept) to open the full product card in a popup. F2 opens the card of the selected line.
AdvTakeposThirdpartyCardPopup = Customer card popup
AdvTakeposThirdpartyCardPopupHelp = Adds an icon after the customer name in the title bar: it opens the third-party card in a popup, directly in edit mode for users allowed to create third parties; the cart is refreshed when it closes. Only shown when a real customer is selected (never for the terminal's default customer). Also adds a pencil on each customer of the register's search list.
AdvTakeposProductCardTab = Tab opened for the product card
AdvTakeposProductCardTabHelp = Tab on which the product card opens in a popup (ⓘ icon of the tiles, reference or info picto of the ticket lines, F2 key). The other tabs stay available in the popup.
AdvTakeposThirdpartyCardTab = Tab opened for the customer card
AdvTakeposThirdpartyCardTabHelp = Tab on which the customer card opens in a popup (card icon next to the customer name). Third party: in edit mode for users allowed to edit third parties. Customer: only for customers and prospects, otherwise the third party card opens.
AdvTakeposCustomerCardBtn = Card
AdvTakeposInitialTariff=Initial price
AdvTakeposTilesNoImage = Tiles without image
AdvTakeposTilesNoImageHelp = For a catalogue without photos: hides the image (crossed-out camera) of product and category tiles; the label fills the whole tile, centred, on the number of lines set above. Screens of 768 px and wider.
AdvTakeposTileLines = Label lines on tiles without image
AdvTakeposTileLinesHelp = Number of product name lines shown on a tile when Tiles without image is enabled (2 to 6). Longer names end with an ellipsis.
AdvTakeposRootCategory = Root category of terminal "%s"
AdvTakeposRootCategoryHelp = Categories shown by this terminal: only the subcategories of the chosen category. Empty = TakePOS setting shared by all terminals. Product search stays open to the whole catalogue.
AdvTakeposLineDescEdit = Line description button
AdvTakeposLineDescEditHelp = Adds a Description button to the action bar: it opens a free text window for the selected line, saved as the invoice line description (as on an order) and printed on the PDF invoice.
AdvTakeposReceiptLineDesc = Description on the receipt
AdvTakeposReceiptLineDescHelp = Prints under each receipt line label the description typed at the till. The description copied from the product card is not printed.
AdvTakeposSendButton = Send button
AdvTakeposSendButtonHelp = Adds a Send button to the action bar: once the sale is paid, it offers to email the invoice as PDF (send form of the invoice card) or the receipt (TakePOS sending, receipt in the email body, template chosen in the TakePOS setup).
AdvTakeposLineDesc = Description
AdvTakeposLineDescTitle = Line description
AdvTakeposLineDescHint = Text saved on the line and printed on the invoice and the receipt.
AdvTakeposLineDescNoLine = Select a receipt line first.
AdvTakeposSend = Send
AdvTakeposSendInvoicePdf = Invoice (PDF)
AdvTakeposSendTicket = Receipt
AdvTakeposSendNeedValidated = The sale must be paid before it can be sent.
AdvTakeposSendNoEmail = No email on the customer card
AdvTakeposSendMailsDisabled = Warning: sending emails is disabled on this instance (MAIN_DISABLE_ALL_MAILS).
AdvTakeposAltBarcodes = Secondary codes for the search
AdvTakeposAltBarcodesHelp = TakePOS only looks for a code in the barcode of the product card. List here, comma separated, the other sources where a scanned code must also find the product: <b>pfp</b> = barcode of supplier prices; <b>ef:field</b> = product extrafield (e.g. ef:ean_kezia); <b>tbl:table:code_column:product_column</b> = mapping table (e.g. tbl:llx_scan_assoc:code:fk_product). The product found is added to the cart as for a card barcode. References (searched word by word, from 2 characters, never added straight to the cart): <b>ref:pfp</b> = supplier reference of supplier prices; <b>ref:ef:field</b> = product extrafield (e.g. ref:ef:ref_fourn_kezia). Empty = disabled.
AdvTakeposPayConfirmOpt = Confirmation before cashing
AdvTakeposPayConfirmOptHelp = In the Payment window, touching a payment mode no longer cashes immediately: a window recalls the mode, the amount, the change to give, the payments already recorded and the remainder to pay, to confirm or correct. The payments already recorded are also shown in the Payment window.
AdvTakeposPayCancelOpt = Cancel the last partial payment
AdvTakeposPayCancelOptHelp = Adds to the Payment window a button that cancels the last payment of a sale not yet fully paid (wrong mode or amount). Same day only, for a user allowed to record payments, if the bank line is not reconciled and the cash desk is not closed. The deletion is traced in the unalterable log (if enabled) and in the technical log. A fully paid sale is corrected with a credit note.
AdvTakeposPayConfirmTitle = Confirm payment
AdvTakeposPayConfirmRefund = Confirm refund
AdvTakeposPayAlready = Already paid
AdvTakeposPayChange = Change to give
AdvTakeposPayRemainAfter = Remainder to pay afterwards
AdvTakeposPayPaidAfter = The sale will be fully paid
AdvTakeposPayDelayed = Validate the sale without payment (delayed payment)
AdvTakeposPayRemain = Remainder to pay
AdvTakeposPayOk = Confirm
AdvTakeposPayBack = Correct
AdvTakeposPayCancel = Cancel last payment
AdvTakeposPayCancelTitle = Cancel this payment?
AdvTakeposPayCancelHint = The sale stays open: the amount is due again.
AdvTakeposPayCancelOk = Cancel payment
AdvTakeposPayCancelNotOpen = Only a payment of a POS sale not yet fully paid can be cancelled.
AdvTakeposPayCancelNone = No payment to cancel.
AdvTakeposPayCancelNotToday = This payment cannot be cancelled from the POS (other day or payment shared with another invoice).
AdvTakeposPayCancelReconciled = This payment is reconciled with the bank: it can no longer be cancelled.
AdvTakeposPayCancelFenceClosed = The cash desk was closed today: the payment can no longer be cancelled.
AdvTakeposPayCancelChanged = The sale has changed: reload the Payment window.
AdvTakeposPayCancelKeep = Keep it
AdvTakeposRestoreCategory = Show the category again after a search
AdvTakeposRestoreCategoryHelp = When the search is cleared (back from payment, input erased), TakePOS leaves an empty grid. With this option, the POS shows the products of the current category again.
AdvTakeposGvOpt = Payment by scanned gift voucher
AdvTakeposGvOptHelp = Requires the GiftVoucher module. In the Payment window, the Gift voucher mode opens a scan window: the POS checks the voucher (valid, already used, expired, cancelled), cashes the applicable amount (the voucher, at most the remainder) and consumes the voucher. If the voucher exceeds the purchase, a new voucher for the rest, with the same validity, is created and printed.
AdvTakeposGvExpiredOpt = Expired gift voucher accepted after confirmation
AdvTakeposGvExpiredOptHelp = An expired voucher scanned at the POS can be accepted with the button "Accept anyway (goodwill)". Disabled: the POS refuses it.
AdvTakeposGvTitle = Gift voucher
AdvTakeposGvHint = Scan the voucher
AdvTakeposGvValid = valid until
AdvTakeposGvApply = Cashed on this sale
AdvTakeposGvRest = Rest (new voucher printed)
AdvTakeposGvOk = Cash the voucher
AdvTakeposGvForce = Accept anyway (goodwill)
AdvTakeposGvClose = Close
AdvTakeposGvUsed = Voucher already used on %s
AdvTakeposGvCanceled = Voucher cancelled
AdvTakeposGvExpired = Voucher expired since %s
AdvTakeposGvNoSale = No sale to pay.
AdvTakeposGvAmountTooHigh = The payment exceeds the amount of voucher %s.
AdvTakeposGvRestNote = Rest of voucher %s (%s used of %s)
AdvTakeposSplitTab = Tab for the pending split sale
AdvTakeposSplitTabHelp = "Split the sale" moves lines to a separate cart that TakePOS never shows among the carts: a split sale left pending becomes invisible. With this option, an orange tab (scissors + amount) appears next to the carts as long as this cart has lines, and opens it in one click.
AdvTakeposSplitTabTitle = Split sale pending since %s (%s line(s))
AdvTakeposLockPaidLines = Paid sale: lines locked
AdvTakeposLockPaidLinesHelp = A validated sale can no longer be modified (Dolibarr silently ignores it). With this option, on a paid sale the line buttons (Qty, Price, Line discount, Description, C, bin) are greyed out and a click shows a message explaining how to correct it.
AdvTakeposLockedSale = Sale %s is paid: its lines can no longer be modified. To correct it, make a return with "Create credit note", or touch "New" to start another sale.
AdvTakeposServiceBadgeOpt = "(S)" (service) instead of stock
AdvTakeposServiceBadgeOptHelp = For an item without stock management (service, or "Stockable product" unchecked), the tile and the cart line show a grey "(S)" instead of a stock of 0.
AdvTakeposServiceBadge = (S)
AdvTakeposServiceBadgeHelp = Item without stock management
AdvTakeposHeaderRemain = Total incl. tax remaining due
AdvTakeposHeaderRemainHelp = In the cart header, "Total incl. tax" becomes "Total incl. tax remaining due": the total minus payments already made (same amount on an unpaid sale, 0 on a fully paid sale).
AdvTakeposTotalRemain = Total incl. tax remaining due
AdvTakeposCreditHelp = Help for credits applied at the POS
AdvTakeposCreditHelpHelp = A credit applied with "Available credits" lowers the total but does not validate the sale. A banner reminds it in the cart until the sale goes through Payment; if the credits cover the whole sale (total 0), the Payment window offers a button "Validate the sale (paid by credits)".
AdvTakeposCreditNotice = Credit applied: the sale is not validated yet. Touch "Payment" to cash the rest.
AdvTakeposCreditNoticeZero = Sale fully covered by credits: touch "Payment" then "Validate the sale (paid by credits)".
AdvTakeposCreditCovered = Validate the sale (paid by credits)
AdvTakeposEditThirdparty = Edit customer card
AdvTakeposCashTerminal = Cash opening: register's terminal enforced
AdvTakeposCashTerminalHelp = With several terminals, the TakePOS cash opening window preselects no terminal. An opening entered for another terminal does not count for this register, which then reopens the window at every start. With this option, the window opened from the register only offers the register's terminal, already selected.
AdvTakeposCashStatus = Cash register status in the header
AdvTakeposCashStatusHelp = Shows next to the terminal name the state of today's cash register: "Register not opened" (click: open it), "Register open" (click: cash report) or "Register closed" (click: cash control card, with the Reopen button). TakePOS does not block sales without an opening, nor after a closing: this indicator makes it visible.
AdvTakeposPopupFit = Cash control windows fitted to their content
AdvTakeposPopupFitHelp = TakePOS opens the cash opening, closing and report windows at a fixed size (90% of the screen). With this option, they take the size of their form, at each step, within the screen.
AdvTakeposPopupEsc = Escape closes the register windows
AdvTakeposPopupEscHelp = The Escape key closes the open window (payment, customers, cash control, cards…), even when the keyboard is inside it. An open drop-down list or confirmation box closes first.
AdvTakeposCashStatusNone = Register not opened
AdvTakeposCashStatusNoneHelp = No cash opening today for this terminal: click to open it
AdvTakeposCashStatusOpen = Register open
AdvTakeposCashStatusOpenHelp = Register opened today: click for the cash report
AdvTakeposCashStatusClosed = Register closed
AdvTakeposCashStatusClosedHelp = Register closed today (sales remain possible): click for the card, with the Reopen button
AdvTakeposCustomerButton = Customer button easy to see
AdvTakeposCustomerButtonHelp = The customer button of the header becomes a filled pill, as high as the cash register status: blue with "Customer" while the sale is on the default customer of the terminal, white with the customer name once a customer is chosen.
AdvTakeposCResetsLine = C button: reset the line to its defaults
AdvTakeposCResetsLineHelp = With input in a popup, the C button resets the selected line as it was added, after confirmation: quantity 1, price and discount computed as when the product is added (customer price, reference price, promo level), product description. Without a selected line, C keeps its native role. A free line has no defaults.
AdvTakeposResetLineConfirm = Reset the line "%s" to its defaults? Quantity 1, starting price and discount, product description.
AdvTakeposResetFreeLine = Free line: it has no defaults to restore.
AdvTakeposCategoryColors = Category colour on their tiles
AdvTakeposCategoryColorsHelp = Category tiles (and sub-category tiles in the product area) take the colour set on the category as background. With tiles without picture, the text turns black or white for contrast. A category without colour keeps the normal background.
AdvTakeposCategoryBreadcrumb = Category breadcrumb
AdvTakeposCategoryBreadcrumbHelp = A breadcrumb (Home › Category › Sub-category) is shown above the category area; each part can be clicked to go back up. A category with sub-categories shows them in place of the categories, and the product area only shows its products (otherwise TakePOS puts the sub-categories first in the product area). The chosen category stays framed. No effect on phones (native category tabs).
AdvTakeposCrumbHome = Home
AdvTakeposSearchCount = Number of products found by the search
AdvTakeposSearchCountHelp = A "57 products" pill is shown at the end of the search field: the total number of products found, all pages included, computed by the search query itself (same filters). It disappears when the search is cleared or a category is chosen.
AdvTakeposSearchCountOne = 1 product
AdvTakeposSearchCountMany = %s products
AdvTakeposSearchNoSoftKeyboard = No on-screen keyboard on the search field (touch screen)
AdvTakeposSearchNoSoftKeyboardHelp = On a touch screen the browser presents as a computer (Chrome on the ELO), TakePOS puts the cursor back in the search field after each click: Android then opens its keyboard and its navigation bar. With this option the cursor stays in the search field (the barcode scanner works) but the keyboard only opens when the Search field is touched; touching elsewhere hides it. No effect on computers without a touch screen.
AdvTakeposSearchSupplier = Search: supplier name
AdvTakeposSearchSupplierHelp = The search bar also finds products by the name (or alias) of one of their suppliers, from the supplier prices. Words are searched one by one: "sakura rod" finds the rods supplied by Sakura even when their label does not say Sakura. Search bar syntax: <b>space</b> = all the words (each one in any field); <b>|</b> = either one (sakura|daiwa); <b>!</b> before a word = without this word (rod !kid); <b>^</b> before = starts with; <b>$</b> after = ends with (^L$ = exactly L); <b>*</b> = any sequence (dpcp*198).
AdvTakeposSearchAttributes = Search: attribute values (variants)
AdvTakeposSearchAttributesHelp = The search bar also finds variants by the values of their attributes (colour, size, power…). A word shorter than 2 characters is searched in the values only when anchored: ^L$. Search bar syntax: <b>space</b> = all the words (each one in any field); <b>|</b> = either one (sakura|daiwa); <b>!</b> before a word = without this word (rod !kid); <b>^</b> before = starts with; <b>$</b> after = ends with (^L$ = exactly L); <b>*</b> = any sequence (dpcp*198).
AdvTakeposSearchFeatures = Search: features (Product features module)
AdvTakeposSearchFeaturesHelp = The search bar also finds products by the values of their features entered with the Product features module (predefined and free values). No effect while that module is disabled. Search bar syntax: <b>space</b> = all the words (each one in any field); <b>|</b> = either one (sakura|daiwa); <b>!</b> before a word = without this word (rod !kid); <b>^</b> before = starts with; <b>$</b> after = ends with (^L$ = exactly L); <b>*</b> = any sequence (dpcp*198).
